___
### Game
calculates Pacman game
___
### SNESpad
provides functions for reading input from SNESpad controllers to be used in "Game"
___
### Graphics
Provides basic functions to write to a bitmap readable by the "display" lib.  
Important: Changing the bitmat doesnt directly affect the display, for the changes to be displayed call "display::refresh()".  

(see [Graphics.h](Graphics/Graphics.h) for more details on the functions)

**clear()**:  
clears whole bitmap 

**fill(color)**:  
fill whole bitmap with a color 

**drawPixel(x,y,color)**:  
set single pixel to one color

**drawRect(x1,y1,x2,y2,color)**:  
draw rectangle of a certain color, calls "drawPixel()" and is therefore not more efficient

**loadImage()**:  
loads image stored in [imageData.h](../include/imageData.h) into the bitmap.   
To generate an imageData.h file use [imageToBitmap.py](../src/imageToBitmap.py) 
>image_to_bitmap_cpp("\<input filename>.png", "\<output filename>")  

(details in .py file)

___
### Display
controls pins on arduino to write to the Display.

**init()**:  
configures Arduino pins, for details on the pins see [Display.cpp](Display/Display.cpp)

**refresh()**:  
Sets physical pins on the arduino according to bitmap provided by "graphics" lib

**enable(en)**:  
Turns whole display on/off